Z||000000||fieroshop||10-20-2000||02:50 AM||||As a second club in the S.F. Bay Area we will be hosting the western regionals with the assistance of Golden Gate Fieros. <BR>We are going to have a drawing on the day of the show in July of 2001. <BR>You need not be present to win. Winner will be responsible for all shipping and all taxes. <BR>Price of tickets is not yet determined but we will post in a day or two.<BR>There will also be an online registration form on our new web site.<BR>Pictures of this car will also be posted soon. Keep a watchful eye for it.<P>------------------<BR> <BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroshop_sig_1.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by fieroshop (edited 10-20-2000).]||||reg||6
Z||000001||fieroshop||10-20-2000||10:53 PM||||Well we have ticket prices for the drawing to be held on the day of the show on July 14th 2001.<BR>For a ten dollar donation you get one ticket. For a fifty dollar donation you get six tickets and for a hundred dollar donation you get fourteen tickets.<P>------------------<BR> <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroshop_sig_1.gif"> ||||reg||10
Z||000002||tgowens||10-21-2000||11:24 AM||||I will post photos of this beautiful car this afternoon!! (By the way George, I want some tickets!!!)<P>------------------<BR>             <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/tgowens_sig.gif">                         <BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A> - Blue '87 GT - Gold '87 GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||tgowens||10-21-2000||05:13 PM||||Here is a picture of the Red '86 SE..... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Red_Fiero_SE.jpg"> .....this is a <B>very clean</B> little car!! The interior is in great shape (not even the usual rip in the driver's seat!!) and will make an excellent car for someone!! More about this car later....<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/tgowens_sig.gif">                          <BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A> - Blue '87 GT - Gold '87 GT<BR><A HREF="http://www.cfog.org" TARGET=_blank>www.cfog.org</A> - Classic Fiero Owners Group||||reg||1
Z||000004||Ozzy||10-21-2000||10:50 PM||||Hey guys....<P>Nice lookin' little rig!<P>Hopefully I'll have my family well settled by then and be able to participate personally. You know, now that I'm down to a single Fiero and all...getting kinda twitchy!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I've been thru both of your towns here in recent weeks but have not had enough time to scratch my butt, let alone stop and find you. All in good time.<P>I'm sitting in Pleasanton Valley medical center at present as I write this due to a major tooth infection...anyone seen the movie "The Elephant Man"? Thats' kinda what I look like. They are pumping all kinds of bug killers into me and as soon as the swelling drops the oral surgeon is gonna rape, pillage and plunder in MY mouth! That is to say I have several major extractions to be done.<P>Moral of the Day!!! <I>Look after yer teeth!</I><P>Ozzy||||reg||10
Z||000005||tgowens||10-22-2000||12:09 AM||||bug killers?? ouch!!! just make sure they don't use brake fluid or motor oil (if they do, make sure it is synthetic - it lasts longer)!!<P>Too bad you didn't have a chance to stop in at the Fiero Shop here in Richmond -- next time you come out this way, call and let me know and we'll "do lunch" <P>Have you decided on a place to park your self and family when you make the move?? I was asking Carolyn the other day if she had heard from you and she hadn't.......(oh, I got a Fiero for her now (that makes three we have now) - an '87 GT 5-speed...........(sure beats that big ol' Benz she drives!!) (only kidding Honey!!)........<P>Take care and stay in touch!<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/tgowens_sig.gif">                          <BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A> - Blue '87 GT - Gold '87 GT<BR><A HREF="http://www.cfog.org" TARGET=_blank>www.cfog.org</A> - Classic Fiero Owners Group||||reg||1
Z||000006||Ozzy||10-22-2000||12:37 AM||||Hey TG...<P>Yeah, I'm sorry too for not having the time. We have some crucial projects right now and big millions riding on 'em so it kinda keeps my mind on the job but, I fully intend on catching up with you guys. <P>I had another e-mail address that is assigned to this registry and I can only get at it from home, consequently, I have not contacted your Better Half!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Again, I do have full intentions of doing this. My wife is down here while I'm layed up and probably her next task is going to be looking around anywhere from Gilroy to SLO. Still vague but that's the way it is right now. We missed out on a place in near Cambria; 3000 sq ft, 4 bd, 2 bth, 100 acres, horse property on the water for $2,700 / mth! You know that did not last long! It must have had some kinda problem; Anything on the water anywhere is usually way over valued!<P>I will call you guys at the shop this week maybe seeing as I have lots of time on my hands between folks stealing my blood and waking me up to put me to sleep!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Ozzy||||reg||10
